{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_10","type":"agent_message","text":"The fused pass exposed a real numerical constraint: Triton’s fast sigmoid differs enough from PyTorch’s sigmoid that the second GEMM amplifies it beyond tolerance. I’m retaining PyTorch’s sigmoid exactly and fusing only the two subsequent multiplies, which still removes one launch and one full intermediate round trip without changing the transcendental implementation."}}
